{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350596-owod-monster-manual","id":1350596,"title":"OWoD monster manual?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-24T00:18:16-08:00","id":1350596,"title":"OWoD monster manual?","content":"Hello, I was wondering if anyone knows of a complete list of all monsters (enemies) for the OWoD game's? )VtM,WtA exe) perhaps a website? I have a bunch of the 2ed/revised books and I'm always piecing together different enemy's for my players, but its a little list from this core book, and a little list from that other book exe. I was wondering if anyone has comprised all of the creatures of the night in one source? I never understood why WW didn't make a monster manual similar to D&amp;D that had all of the monsters from all the different games thought all of the game time periods.<br /> \u200b Any help would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25760-walks-through-sewage","name":"Walks Through Sewage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25760_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T01:31:01-08:00","id":1350602,"title":"","content":"That's probably because the monsters are the PCs. &quot;Enemies&quot; aren't enemies by default like in D&amp;D. A monster manual that provides a statblock and limited &quot;ecology&quot; section has less place in a setting that's more predicated on social interaction than combat, and has a smaller variety of critters running around anyway. <br /> <br /> Your best bet, regardless, is probably the White Wolf Wiki. You might start on the articles for Kindred, Garou, mages, and all the other major races.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T02:33:21-08:00","id":1350611,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of it goes back to Vampire being primarily a game about social and political interactions between various vampires, and its book structure setting the template for the other lines. For Werewolf, back in the day, the original Book of the Wyrm and later Freak Legion were the closest thing to D&amp;D style monster manuals. There was also Axis Mundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T03:40:03-08:00","id":1350620,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone's bothered because all the game lines use different rules. A general &quot;Monster Manual&quot; style book with a fomori in it doesn't do you any good unless you have the WtA books, or reprint all the fomori rules in the manual. This means the entries are going to either being (a) obnoxiously long or (b) only useful to people that have all the books anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:25:16-08:00","id":1350725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350596-owod-monster-manual?p=1350611#post1350611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of it goes back to Vampire being primarily a game about social and political interactions between various vampires, and its book structure setting the template for the other lines. For Werewolf, back in the day, the original Book of the Wyrm and later Freak Legion were the closest thing to D&amp;D style monster manuals. There was also Axis Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Axis Mundi, that's one of the books I don't have, thank you, I'm sure this will help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25760-walks-through-sewage","name":"Walks Through Sewage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25760_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:50:48-08:00","id":1350731,"title":"","content":"If anyone else is wondering I have found a few online sources (WtA)(VtM) This is more of what I had in mind, not so much all the stats (those are easy for a ST to creat) but more of an in-game canon list. This is not nearly all of it but its a step in the direction that I was asking about. Thank you all for the replies. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://romanbode.wixsite.com/werewolf/bad-guys-roll-call\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/507ffa_aecf9a68d7834db692d5b7857ff73664.jpg/v1/fill/w_288,h_162,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,blur_2,enc_avif,quality_auto/507ffa_aecf9a68d7834db692d5b7857ff73664.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://romanbode.wixsite.com/werewolf/bad-guys-roll-call\" target=\"_blank\"> Enemies of the Garou | werewolf </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://romanbode.wixsite.com/werewolf/bad-guys-roll-call\" target=\"_blank\"> https://romanbode.wixsite.com/werewolf/bad-guys-roll-call </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Paul Bode, Werewolf the Apocalypse, Word of Darkness, campaign, fan made, role play, role-play, roleplay </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://vtmr.fandom.com/wiki/Creature_list\" target=\"_blank\">https://vtmr.fandom.com/wiki/Creature_list</a> from the Video game but it helps<br /> If anyone knows of any more sources go ahead and link them up<br /> Thanks again.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"